{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734684",
      "title": "Working with State",
      "sourceHash": "d4597225a19c277f91264ed69e2c0d7d7217dab415e40e66e7262f3e6abed574",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.087,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "So now we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "how we can set up event listeners.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 8.7,
          "en": "Let's now dive into this state concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 12.18,
          "en": "And to get started, I simply wanna output the text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.18,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "that's input into this textarea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 17.403,
          "en": "in a new paragraph below this input in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "We'll soon also make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.9,
          "en": "that it ends up in the post component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 24.213,
          "en": "but for the moment let's just output it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.59,
          "end": 29.31,
          "en": "To achieve this, we need to store the value somewhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "and then reference that somewhere down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "And the first thing you might think about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 38.13,
          "en": "could be a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "We could add a variable enteredBody",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 43.563,
          "en": "which maybe is an empty string initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 47.76,
          "en": "And then here instead of console logging the entered value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.76,
          "end": 52.44,
          "en": "we could store it as a value in enteredBody like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "So we update the variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "whenever this function is executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 59.103,
          "en": "which happens on every keystroke as we saw.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 62.82,
          "en": "And then we could use this enteredBody variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.82,
          "end": 65.07,
          "en": "down there in this paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "So here we can use our single curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 70.923,
          "en": "and output enteredBody.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "So this variable is updated here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "and is then output down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 80.253,
          "en": "Should work, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 83.26,
          "en": "Well, if you save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 88.71000000000001,
          "en": "and you type something here, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.71000000000001,
          "end": 90.6,
          "en": "It should be output down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 93.45,
          "en": "because that's where I added the paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.45,
          "end": 96.12,
          "en": "And indeed, if you inspect this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.12,
          "end": 99.66,
          "en": "you will see that below this textarea here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.66,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "is an empty paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 103.983,
          "en": "but it is indeed that, empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.85,
          "end": 108.66,
          "en": "What I type here is not being output in that paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.66,
          "end": 109.91,
          "en": "Now why is that the case?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 112.8,
          "en": "Well because there is something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.8,
          "end": 115.2,
          "en": "very important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.2,
          "end": 119.75999999999999,
          "en": "React executes your component functions like NewPost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "and it then takes the JSX code returned by those functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 126.87,
          "en": "So the current snapshot of the HTML content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.87,
          "end": 128.94,
          "en": "that should be output on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.94,
          "end": 131.613,
          "en": "and it does render it to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "But if thereafter in your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 138.27,
          "en": "you change some variable value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.27,
          "end": 140.73,
          "en": "that's being used in your JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.73,
          "end": 143.7,
          "en": "that won't be picked up by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 148.35,
          "en": "because this JSX code is only taken once as a snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 151.743,
          "en": "when this component function is executed for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.95,
          "en": "Indeed, if that component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 157.56,
          "en": "would be executed by a React again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.56,
          "end": 161.28,
          "en": "it would also consider any updates to that snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.28,
          "end": 164.07,
          "en": "and update the rendered user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "But React does by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 170.55,
          "en": "not randomly execute NewPost again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 173.25,
          "en": "And it does not execute NewPost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.25,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "or any other component function again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 177.87,
          "en": "just because you changed some variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "or just because you have some event listener in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 183.3,
          "en": "This is ignored by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.3,
          "end": 185.22,
          "en": "Of course it adds the event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.22,
          "end": 188.25,
          "en": "and this function executes, but it does not care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 192.483,
          "en": "about whether this would theoretically change your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.8,
          "end": 198.15,
          "en": "Instead, you have to basically create this variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.15,
          "end": 201.32999999999998,
          "en": "in a special way using a special React feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.32999999999998,
          "end": 203.94,
          "en": "to let React know about any changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.94,
          "end": 206.403,
          "en": "that should cause a UI update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.48,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "And for that you have to import something from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "So from the React library, not from React DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 216.84300000000002,
          "en": "but from just React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.71,
          "end": 222.123,
          "en": "And that something is a function called useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.68,
          "end": 226.5,
          "en": "Now this is a so called React Hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 228.84,
          "en": "React has multiple built-in functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 230.76,
          "en": "that all start with use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.76,
          "end": 233.22,
          "en": "as you can see here with my auto completion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.22,
          "end": 234.9,
          "en": "And these functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.9,
          "end": 239.01,
          "en": "whilst technically being standard JavaScript functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.01,
          "end": 240.993,
          "en": "are called React Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.89,
          "end": 244.74,
          "en": "So functions in React that start with use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.74,
          "end": 247.41,
          "en": "are considered React Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.41,
          "end": 250.71,
          "en": "The special thing about these hook functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.71,
          "end": 255.15,
          "en": "is that you must execute them inside of component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.15,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "You can't execute them in regular JavaScript functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "You can, but you'll get a warning or an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 263.52,
          "en": "But you must execute them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.52,
          "end": 266.1,
          "en": "in React component functions instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.1,
          "end": 269.43,
          "en": "And then those hook functions typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 272.79,
          "en": "change something about that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.79,
          "end": 276.843,
          "en": "or regarding how React behaves with that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "In case of useState when you execute that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 283.38,
          "en": "inside of a component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 283.38,
          "end": 287.37,
          "en": "you register a new state slice, as you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.37,
          "end": 291.513,
          "en": "A new state value that belongs to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.35,
          "end": 294.96,
          "en": "In a state value can be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.96,
          "end": 298.11,
          "en": "It can be an object, a number, an array, a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.11,
          "end": 299.94,
          "en": "whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.94,
          "end": 303.75,
          "en": "Here if you wanna store the entered text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 303.75,
          "end": 307.44,
          "en": "we could register a string as a state slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 307.44,
          "end": 308.853,
          "en": "for this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.87,
          "end": 314.13,
          "en": "You set a default value for that state variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 314.13,
          "end": 315.81,
          "en": "if you want to call it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 315.81,
          "end": 320.55,
          "en": "by passing your initial value as an argument to useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 320.55,
          "end": 324.54,
          "en": "For example an empty string just as I did it down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 324.54,
          "end": 326.13,
          "en": "But again, that could be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 326.13,
          "end": 329.37,
          "en": "It can be undefined, it can be a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.37,
          "end": 331.983,
          "en": "it could be an object, but here it's a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.113,
          "end": 337.86,
          "en": "useState then returns something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.86,
          "end": 340.40999999999997,
          "en": "It returns an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 342.39,
          "en": "And I'll store that array in a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342.39,
          "end": 346.593,
          "en": "StateData is a name we could use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 347.82,
          "end": 350.19,
          "en": "Now this stateData array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 350.19,
          "end": 354.06,
          "en": "has always exactly two elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 354.06,
          "end": 356.64300000000003,
          "en": "never more, never less.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 357.78,
          "end": 360.6,
          "en": "And the first element of stateData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 360.6,
          "end": 363.33,
          "en": "is always the current state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 363.33,
          "end": 365.37,
          "en": "So initially that empty string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 365.37,
          "end": 368.733,
          "en": "but that value can change as you will soon see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 369.84,
          "end": 374.4,
          "en": "Because that second element in that stateData array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 374.4,
          "end": 377.16,
          "en": "is a state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.16,
          "end": 381.45,
          "en": "A function which you can execute to assign a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 381.45,
          "end": 383.28,
          "en": "to your state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 383.28,
          "end": 385.53,
          "en": "Because that state value is stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 388.47,
          "en": "somewhere in memory by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 388.47,
          "end": 390.54,
          "en": "You set an initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 390.54,
          "end": 392.49,
          "en": "and you can then call this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 392.49,
          "end": 395.79,
          "en": "which is returned by useState as a second element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 395.79,
          "end": 400.23,
          "en": "in this stateData array to update that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 400.23,
          "end": 402.87,
          "en": "Now the special thing about that is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 402.87,
          "end": 406.14,
          "en": "that if you call that state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 406.14,
          "end": 410.67,
          "en": "you don't just store a new value somewhere in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 410.67,
          "end": 415.29,
          "en": "but React will also reexecute that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 415.29,
          "end": 417.63,
          "en": "in which this state was registered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 417.63,
          "end": 422.1,
          "en": "So it will call this component function again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 422.1,
          "end": 425.85,
          "en": "just as it did initially when it rendered that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 425.85,
          "end": 427.86,
          "en": "for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 427.86,
          "end": 431.25,
          "en": "And since it calls that component function again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 431.25,
          "end": 433.23,
          "en": "you get the current state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 433.23,
          "end": 435.09,
          "en": "So the value which you just set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 435.09,
          "end": 437.43,
          "en": "with help of that state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 437.43,
          "end": 439.92,
          "en": "as the first element here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 439.92,
          "end": 442.95,
          "en": "And you get the latest JSX snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 442.95,
          "end": 444.63,
          "en": "And if that deviates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 444.63,
          "end": 448.2,
          "en": "from the previously rendered JSX snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 448.2,
          "end": 453.2,
          "en": "React will update the parts in the UI that need updating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 453.51,
          "end": 455.76,
          "en": "And that's, by the way, all important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 455.76,
          "end": 458.85,
          "en": "React will basically make a comparison",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 458.85,
          "end": 461.55,
          "en": "between the different snapshots behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 461.55,
          "end": 465.65999999999997,
          "en": "and only update the parts in the UI that must be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 465.65999999999997,
          "end": 469.29,
          "en": "so that you don't unnecessarily update the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 469.29,
          "end": 471.873,
          "en": "which is quite performance intensive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 473.22,
          "end": 475.77,
          "en": "So that's what you get back here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 475.77,
          "end": 478.8,
          "en": "Now it's quite common to use array destructuring here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 478.8,
          "end": 482.64,
          "en": "which is a default modern JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 482.64,
          "end": 485.94,
          "en": "to store the current value in a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 485.94,
          "end": 489.24,
          "en": "and the updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 489.24,
          "end": 491.43,
          "en": "And typically you should pick names here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 491.43,
          "end": 493.14,
          "en": "that describe your state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 493.14,
          "end": 495.84,
          "en": "like for example, the enteredBody.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 495.84,
          "end": 497.43,
          "en": "And then the updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 497.43,
          "end": 499.98,
          "en": "could be called setEnteredbody.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 499.98,
          "end": 501.78,
          "en": "It's kind of a convention to name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 501.78,
          "end": 504.12,
          "en": "this state updating function set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 504.12,
          "end": 506.91,
          "en": "and then you basically repeat your state name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 506.91,
          "end": 509.103,
          "en": "just format it as camel case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 510.27,
          "end": 512.73,
          "en": "Now I'll remove that variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 512.73,
          "end": 515.7,
          "en": "because we have a name clash otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 515.7,
          "end": 518.703,
          "en": "And with that we registered this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 519.84,
          "end": 521.55,
          "en": "Now to update that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 521.55,
          "end": 524.19,
          "en": "you don't try to assign a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 524.19,
          "end": 528.36,
          "en": "That's why I also use the const here for these two values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 528.36,
          "end": 530.34,
          "en": "Because instead you have to call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 530.34,
          "end": 534.81,
          "en": "this state updating function, setEnteredBody,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 534.81,
          "end": 537.66,
          "en": "like this and pass your new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 537.66,
          "end": 541.623,
          "en": "as a value for this argument to setEnteredBody.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 542.7,
          "end": 545.43,
          "en": "Then behind the scenes, the new state value is stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 545.43,
          "end": 547.8,
          "en": "and this component function is executed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 547.8,
          "end": 551.4,
          "en": "and enteredBody will then hold that new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 551.4,
          "end": 553.32,
          "en": "That's why it may be a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 553.32,
          "end": 555.42,
          "en": "because it's always a brand new constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 555.42,
          "end": 558.3,
          "en": "because it's always a brand new function execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 558.3,
          "end": 560.553,
          "en": "in the end when you update the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 561.45,
          "end": 564.84,
          "en": "So now we can use this enteredBody state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 564.84,
          "end": 569.22,
          "en": "in this paragraph to output the new state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 569.22,
          "end": 572.55,
          "en": "But this time because we're using this state feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 572.55,
          "end": 576.18,
          "en": "provided by React with help of the useState hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 576.18,
          "end": 578.31,
          "en": "this will all work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 578.31,
          "end": 580.74,
          "en": "And if I now save everything again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 580.74,
          "end": 583.68,
          "en": "you will see that as I type something here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 583.68,
          "end": 587.43,
          "en": "it updates down there below the text input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 587.43,
          "end": 589.08,
          "en": "So this works now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 589.08,
          "end": 594.08,
          "en": "And with every keystroke this gets updated as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 594.84,
          "end": 598.113,
          "en": "Now that's Reacts state feature in action.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
